<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Do-Aklin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 1600</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Do-Aklin is remembered in the traditions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-dahomey">Dahomey</a> as the leader of the royal family that migrated from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allada">Allada</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abomey">Abomey</a> plateau around 1600, after a succession dispute in the Kingdom of Allada. He is regarded as the ancestor and first chief of the line that later founded the kingdom, though historians treat these early traditions with caution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/do-aklin.jpg" alt="Do-Aklin" width="320" height="279" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adoscam · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Symbole_de_Gangnihessou_roi_du_Dahomey_au_mur_de_la_place_Goho_%C3%A0_Abomey_au_B%C3%A9nin_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
